The acute case is the circumcenter on the bisector; in the obtuse case the midpoint of the longest edge includes zero and attains half that edge length. If $E=1/2+\tau<\sqrt2/2$, the obtuse branch is excluded, and the acute expression bounds each color's chordal diameter by $O(\sqrt\tau)$. Its directions lie in a cap of area $O(\tau)$. Covering the sphere needs at least $c/\tau$ colors, hence at least $\log_2(1/\tau)-O(1)$ complete bits. This all-size lower does not assert a uniform lower at each fixed finite $N$.

